From 7aa53d4997a7efd7bef4e7ffec7e4b4cee6ca8d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miures Manager <contact@miures.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:41:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Research Engine Phase 1 (reliability): the model path says
 exactly why; the research design is editable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

From the Research Engine audit (docs/RESEARCH-ENGINE-AUDIT-2026-10-08.md, section K, Phase 1).

Model path (packages/ai): completeJson reads finish_reason and continues an
answer cut off at max_tokens (continuations, default 2, metered per call);
a prose reply is asked for once more as the object alone; what still cannot
be read is thrown as AiReplyError (truncated / unparseable / empty) instead
of returning null. A schema is sent as response_format: json_schema where
the provider takes it, with a remembered fallback to json_object or plain;
an unrelated 400 is not retried.

Studio: lib/copilot/failure.ts — every failure of the model path has a code,
a title, the cause and the next steps (not_configured, wallet, timeout,
provider, network, truncated, unparseable, empty, unusable). The route
returns it on 501, 402/423, 502 and the unusable-reply body; the copilot
card shows it with "What to do" and what the engine had read before it
handed the sentence on. The grammar's "I did not understand that" no longer
replaces a model failure: an empty answer still reaches the grammar, which
is offered when it reads the phrasing and otherwise leaves the failed turn
as the answer. The engine-only card names the missing model (AI_API_URL),
the sentences the engine reads and what it read; "NOT UNDERSTOOD" is gone.

Configuration: .env.example documents the AI_* variables; lib/aiConfig.ts
reports presence only (ai, aiFake, aiModel) with warnings on /platform.

Analytics: buildFor adds the plan's derived variables and segments to every
dataset (idempotent second pass; an uncomputable variable leaves its note on
the results that read it); milestone runs use the clean dataset and the
stored run carries its dataset spec; factor analysis outputs its scores (a
per-factor table and per-case scores in dataset order — factorAnalysis now
returns the scored cases' indices, null for a case missing an item); dead
significanceLetters removed.

Research design editor (components/studio/ResearchDesignEditor.tsx):
objective, population, methodology, planned completes, hypotheses with
coverage chips, constructs with role / definition / measuring questions,
assumptions — in Survey Settings and the Analysis tab. Removing a
hypothesis goes through the engine's remove_hypothesis so the H-tags on
questions and plan items are renumbered.

Tests: packages/ai reply.test.ts (4), apps/studio failure.test.ts (4) and
platformAi.test.ts (3), packages/analytics phase1.test.ts (3), browser
scripts/phase1-reliability-test.mjs (9 checks); intelligent-mode and
copilot suites updated for the failed turn with its cause. Mutation checks:
ai 12/12, analytics 9/9, failure + aiConfig 12/12, Studio surfaces 10/10.
Full corpus: 119 ok; the 9 failures are the known baseline (4 need
Postgres, 5 unchanged from the previous run). pnpm -r test green (17
packages), both typechecks and the auth-guard audit clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
